worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:19:- **Hypothesis** — Exact ties at the maximum are rare and depth can be recovered exactly from the point cloud.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:24:  - **Per-pixel L2 norm of the point cloud is NOT rotation-invariant bitwise** (300/300 mismatches after `rotate_scene_metadata`; the rotation matrix is float32-built), but **`depth = z / (−sin φ_row)` IS** (0/300 mismatches): the z channel is untouched by a rotation about z, and `sin φ_row` is a per-row constant. `min_row |sin φ| = 0.00614`, never zero. Recovered depth matches the raw `.npy` to 8.9e-16 (91 % of pixels bitwise).
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:25:- **Analysis** — A literal argmax-first rule would canonicalize 3.75 % of panoramas rotation-dependently (frame jumps up to 80°), contradicting the invariance claim on ~240 of the 6,337 unseen items. The plan therefore proposes (D1) an equivariant tie-break on the exactly-recovered profile (plan §2.1), with the literal rule as the alternative for Yixun to choose.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:31:- **Result** — Both A6000s hold a `train_xRIR_backbone.py` process each (cwd `~/codespace/xRIR_code_wt13`, exp13_cylvit_rope seeds 0/1 — Yixun's xRIR project, NOT this worktree; never touched): ~32.5 GB used per GPU. seed0 (pid 3659396, started Oct 22 07:58) is in its last epoch (11/12) → frees GPU 0 within the hour; seed1 (pid 294846, started Oct 23 15:38) is in epoch 1/12 at ≈175 min/epoch → ETD ≈ **2026-10-25 03:00 EDT** (earlier if it speeds up once seed0 exits). The reviewed P1/exp_17 launch gate requires ≥ 21,900 MiB free per GPU (rank ≈ 15.7 GiB measured + DDP/SyncBN allowance); GPU 1 has ≈ 16.5 GiB free until seed1 ends.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:45:- **Result** — `depth_canon_codex_plan_review.md` (gpt-5.6-sol xhigh, 117 lines): **REVISE** — BLOCKING B1 residual-tie path not equivariant + depth-only audit insufficient; B2 checkpoint/config binding not fail-closed; B3 invariance evidence/thresholds too loose and `--store_predictions` saves pre-clamp tensors (announcement 08 unmet). HIGH H4 "exact recovery" overstated; H5 random-yaw comparison not four-arm; H6 `model_comparison.md` carries the exp_15 (neuronic) Yaw-Aug row, not exp_17's; H7 single-delta is a historical matched-recipe claim; H8 missing tests; H9 launcher needs run-owned-checkpoint + NAS gates. NIT N10 naming, N11 cost wording. Verified correct: roll direction/sign, `z = −D sin φ` recovery formula, equivariance of the rooted lexicographic key, placement at all dispatch sites and after `apply_rotation_plan`, pose co-rotation physics, exclusions, recipe trace, the planning probe (as a probe).
