worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_worklog.md:153:- **Analysis** — Deviation (disclosed, closest faithful): the hash normalizes signed zeros so that equal proxies hash equal; canonical outputs are always post-rotation (the einsum writes `+0.0`), so for AR (min depth ≈ 0.26 m, no zero pixels) the literal and normalized hashes coincide; the normalization only matters for zero-depth inputs (e.g. other datasets) or for hashing a never-rotated cloud. Cost per sample ≈ 3.8 ms (24 threads) / 10 ms (1 thread) → at 32 samples/rank/step ≈ 0.12–0.33 s on CPU vs ≈ 3.9 s per optimizer step for P1 (0.259 step/s), i.e. ≈ 3–8 % if run serially in the training step — to be measured at the round-2 smoke.
